mmary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro is reportedly on the way to the US, according to reports citing people close to the senator. Bolsonaro's passports were canceled earlier Tuesday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU proposes giving Frontex border agency new major powers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d07f634d0ac53411bf2ff75e1e4c250f0a54adca95a8186d5f83327979871524</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-giving-frontex-border-agency-new-major-powers/a-79779690--2177a1c8ad5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-giving-frontex-border-agency-new-major-powers/a-79779690?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has unveiled a new plan to give Frontex more resources to ensure the return of irregular migrants, including by supporting non-EU countries. The move comes after the tragedy in Ceuta.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mbappe apologizes as Chinese sponsors drop him and TV broadcasts are halted over Mao dictator remark</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:083b4097fbc485a5d3e300e74802820ffff2bdba10b41d8dae0f1f8c8e0ec306</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831--140a68dc18a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mbappe-apologizes-as-chinese-sponsors-drop-him-and-tv-broadcasts-are-halted-over-mao-dictator-remark/a-79779831?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French soccer star Kylian Mbappe has apologized after apparently referring to Mao Zedong as a dictator. Chinese sponsors have dropped him, while state television has suspended Spanish league broadcasts.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar: Is the US undermining the EU's diplomatic blockade?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e10d8aed82ff1e8466763c917de11a7108685303f746befac393b15715c03742</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:49:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863--db2dea3e5776.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-is-the-us-undermining-the-eu-s-diplomatic-blockade/a-79778863?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With the US reopening talks with Myanmar's military-backed government, and several Southeast Asian countries restarting diplomatic contacts, the EU is facing uncomfortable questions about its own boycott of the junta.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4178a155c407ed7820c4ffa6c0dcdc47b65e4a9b251f9980ad7b611ebf296b80</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd88968447adafde6b8e27a7b44ccae39a59d5d5bdd29a901d782116fc102cba</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Denmark's Frederiksen criticizes Finland and Norway for calling Putin without coordinating with allies, despite consultation with Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93694549088f239b91a9a1d5c47fb44aeeeec06441a88e5fac188a7de69d1006</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/denmark-s-frederiksen-criticizes-finland-and-norway-for-calling-putin-without-coordinating-with-alli/a-79776208--b9062a9ff501.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/denmark-s-frederiksen-criticizes-finland-and-norway-for-calling-putin-without-coordinating-with-allies-despite-consultation-with-ukraine/a-79776208?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland and Norway have called Putin about ending the Ukraine war, drawing Danish criticism. The dispute highlights divisions over European engagement with Moscow ahead of planned US-led peace talks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan acknowledges civilian casualties in Syria airstrike against 'Islamic State'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e2261c4ef39cc21a2f60cda0d3b552ac3a98b9a09d01daed686230c1ba55386</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jordan-acknowledges-civilian-casualties-in-syria-airstrike-against-islamic-state/a-79775653--7282e0a35d06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jordan-acknowledges-civilian-casualties-in-syria-airstrike-against-islamic-state/a-79775653?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Jordanian government spokesman has expressed "regret" over civilian casualties in an airstrike it said was targeting "IS" militants.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo reports over 10,000 Ebola cases as the outbreak spreads abroad, with no approved vaccine or specific treatment for the Bundibugyo virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a86d267ccf38318b6f5c077937b13d252ec4524579263ba2bb0d91c82bb2c4c8</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-reports-over-10-000-ebola-cases-as-the-outbreak-spreads-abroad-with-no-approved-vaccine-or-/a-79773667--055ba7810ea4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-reports-over-10-000-ebola-cases-as-the-outbreak-spreads-abroad-with-no-approved-vaccine-or-specific-treatment-for-the-bundibugyo-virus/a-79773667?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DR Congo has reported more than 10,000 Ebola cases and nearly 4,900 deaths. The outbreak involves a virus for which there is no approved vaccine or specific treatment, complicating efforts to contain its spread.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz says erosion of global order means middle powers in Europe and Asia must be more assertive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:198ecafbb19a93cf6d4c2f381d4ac425573905bd1966ffc0633f0b3b13944580</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-asse/live-79772992--98272a034e7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-assertive/live-79772992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a visit to Singapore, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said Europe and Germany want to increase free trade with open competition, reliability and a rules-based order.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two men face UK national security charges following an incident near RAF Fairford, with police suspecting Iranian state involvement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19d1a363eee8400e326663bcd2637f72fd211cdd8474173fcbbd9915731e3c73</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T09:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-men-face-uk-national-security-charges-following-an-incident-near-raf-fairford-with-police-suspec/a-79773432--5ee211ad289a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-men-face-uk-national-security-charges-following-an-incident-near-raf-fairford-with-police-suspecting-iranian-state-involvement/a-79773432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">British prosecutors have charged two men over an incident near RAF Fairford in September. Police suspect Iranian involvement in the case at a base used for US strikes on Iran.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Police in northern Germany search for suspects after car ramming overnight injures several</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfdb620eb311e0fcb7e23eba5d0c28859e4c7c0fe72202715b16453e2c07753d</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T07:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/police-in-northern-germany-search-for-suspects-after-car-ramming-overnight-injures-several/a-78107062--249602b37b60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/police-in-northern-germany-search-for-suspects-after-car-ramming-overnight-injures-several/a-78107062?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A person intentionally drove into a group of people in a northern German town, police have said. Three people have been taken into custody in what police said was likely a gang confrontation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Arunachal sees fresh violence over proposed dam</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7aab5aa480c7ef853f2475877b006a9413bdca943595ea061aea31c7f6fa735</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650--d59bfea6f557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-arunachal-sees-fresh-violence-over-proposed-dam/live-79771650?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More violence erupted in India's northeastern state of Arunachal Pradesh over proposed hydroelectric projects that locals are protesting. Also, India's top court will hear pleas against the poll body chief.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil elections: Merz, world leaders congratulate Lula on his win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1244b7d41010d5da031e1a3a3ee25ccab2f2777151624485d53022ab364b1b39</id><updated>2026-10-27T20:48:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T04:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-elections-merz-world-leaders-congratulate-lula-on-his-win/live-79755630--42141a0af1cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-elections-merz-world-leaders-congratulate-lula-on-his-win/live-79755630?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Lula secured a surprise win over far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, whose party recognizes Lula's election victory.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine and Russia begin Oleshky ceasefire for aid mission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:824532ce